remstart
    EXTINCT. (Chris, 2026-11-07.) the routines are in fish_routines_extinct, and the tests in fish_tests_extinct.

    WHEN A KIND GOES. when a look at the board pops the last fish of one of the seven kinds that a game
    starts with, or of the jellyfish or the stingrays, so that not one of that kind is left on the
    board, that kind is extinct. it goes up onto THE LADDER, beside the board, and from then on no new
    fish of that kind drops in. the bottles, the quest kinds and the diver never go (extinctCanGo). a
    kind that is on the ladder already does not go again. the jellyfish and the
    stingrays are there so that a game with their cards has more kinds to get rid of.

    BACK ACROSS THE BOARD. a kind that comes off of the ladder by a swap, to the right or to the left,
    is put back onto the board spread out (Chris, 2026-11-07), so that it is hard to get rid of again:
    about one fish in five, in the cells that a knight's move apart from one another (x + 2y, every
    EXTINCT_SEED_EVERY), so that none of them touch, and none of them pop. a fish of the kind is not put
    next to one that is there already. only plain fish are turned: not a quest's kind, the diver or a
    bottle. it waits for the board to be still, and after a flip, for its pops to be over
    (EXTINCT_SEED_KIND, extinctSeedStep). the kinds that a missed swap sends back are not spread.
    every fish that is turned turns over like a card, one after another across the board: it goes
    thin, is the new kind when it is edge on, and comes back around (Chris, 2026-11-07). nothing can be
    moved while they turn (extinctSeedTurnStep).

    THE FLOOR. a kind does not go if that would leave fewer than EXTINCT_FLOOR kinds dropping in
    (extinctDropping). with three rungs it is never reached; it is there for a ladder with more. extinctJudgePops, from
    handle_combos, sees it, once the fish have fallen and before the new ones are picked. it is off on
    the little boards of the tutorial, in a puzzle and in a demo, and while the board flips (THE FLIP).

    THE LADDER. three rungs, up the left side of the board, from the bottom row up, one row in two (rows
    8, 6 and 4 of the first board), so that there is an empty row between one rung and the next, and
    nothing can be slid from one to another (Chris, 2026-11-07). the first kind to go is on the bottom
    rung, and the next one on the rung above. a fourth kind cannot go while three are up: it pops off of
    the board like any other, and keeps coming.

    A MISS SENDS THEM BACK. a swap that pops nothing, and is held against the player (the same swaps that
    cost the multiplier, in judgeMultiplierSwaps), sends every kind on the ladder back, for nothing: they
    come off of it and drop in again (extinctSwapMissed). they are not used, so they can go up again.
    so a full ladder takes three kinds wiped out without one
    wasted swap, which most likely takes cards (Chris, 2026-11-07).
    the ladder is drawn in stepExtinct, the same way as the pickup of a quest, and the cursor steps out
    onto a rung from the cell beside it, the same way too (THE CURSOR STEPS OFF OF THE BOARD, in
    fish_headers_quests): SELECTION_POS stays on the cell beside the rung, and EXTINCT_CURSOR_OUT says
    which rung the cursor is drawn out on. out there, a step right comes back in, a swap right is THE
    FLIP, and a swap left is THE LEFT SWAP. nothing else does anything.

    THE FLIP. swapping a rung right, onto the board, spins part of the board over (THE SPIN), and it
    comes back around with every fish on it turned into that kind. they all pop, with the multiplier as
    it is. how much of the board goes with the rung (Chris, 2026-11-07, so that the bottom rung is not a
    jackpot): the row that the rung is beside, and every row under it, so the bottom rung turns one row
    and the middle one three. the top one turns the whole board, which is most likely the end of the
    round, though it does not end it on its own (extinctFlipRows). the kind comes off of the ladder, and new
    fish of it drop in again. every fish, the kinds of the cards and bottles too, is turned; quest kinds
    and the diver are not, and a fish that is belly up, or a skeleton, is a plain fish again. it waits
    for the board to be still, and it does nothing at night, when nothing pops (the cursor shakes).

    THE LEFT SWAP. swapping a rung left, off of the board, lets its kind go in place of a flip, and gets
    something else for it, which is more the higher the rung is. what it gets is written in the box to
    the left of the rung, so that it looks like what the swap is for (Chris, 2026-11-08):
    - the bottom rung has none, and no box. the cursor shakes.
    - the middle rung doubles the multiplier (EXTINCT_LEFT_TIMES, which can triple it too, for a ladder
      with more rungs). its kind comes back, the same as after a flip.
    - the top rung halves the moves of the game so far (Chris, 2026-11-08: big, but nothing that stays
      changed). they come off of the counter one at a time with the dings of the negative moves card
      (PENDING_FREE_MOVES, frame_free_moves). only its own kind comes back; the rungs under it stay
      (Chris, 2026-11-09).

    WHEN A RUNG IS USED, the rungs above it slide down one, so there is never a gap in the ladder.

    WHEN THE ROUND ENDS, nothing happens to the ladder (Chris, 2026-11-07). what is on it stays on it, round
    after round, until it is used.

    NEW FISH. getRandomValue, in fish_funcs, picks a new fish from the kinds that are not out
    (extinctPick). while none are out, it rolls the stream just as it did before there was a ladder, so
    a seed plays the same up to the first kind that goes. the fish from the schools are left out too.

    THE SAVED GAME keeps the rungs, from EXTINCT_PREF.

    STILL TO DO. no codex entry, angler line or achievement yet. the fish of a quest's own idea of what
    drops in (questNewFish) can still be a kind that is out.
remend

global EXTINCT_ON = 1 `0 turns it off, for the tests
global EXTINCT_RUNGS = 3 `how many rungs the ladder has
global EXTINCT_TOP_KIND = 15 `the highest kind that the arrays below have room for. extinctCanGo says which of them can go.
global dim EXTINCT_RUNG(6) `the kind on every rung, from the bottom one up, or 0 for none
global dim EXTINCT_BORN_MS(6) `when the kind on every rung went up onto it
global dim EXTINCT_DRAWN_Y#(6) `where every rung is drawn, which slides down to its row when a rung under it is used
global dim EXTINCT_OUT(16) `1 for every kind that does not drop in: one that is on the ladder
global EXTINCT_OUT_COUNT = 0 `how many kinds are out
global EXTINCT_PICKED = 1 `the kind that extinctPick picked
global EXTINCT_KINDS = 7 `the first seven kinds, which every game starts with
global dim EXTINCT_SEED_KIND(16) `1 for every kind that is waiting to be put back across the board. see BACK ACROSS THE BOARD.
global EXTINCT_SEED_EVERY = 5 `one cell in this many gets the kind back
global EXTINCT_SEED_MS = -1 `when the fish of a spread started to turn over, or -1 when none are
global EXTINCT_SEED_TURN_TIME = 300 `how long one fish takes to turn over, in milliseconds
global EXTINCT_SEED_STAGGER = 30 `and how long after the one before it each one starts
global EXTINCT_SEED_COUNT = 0 `how many fish are turning over
global EXTINCT_SEED_KIND_TO = 0 `the kind that they turn into
global dim EXTINCT_SEED_CELL(160) `the cells that are turning, in the order that they turn
global dim EXTINCT_SEED_TURNED(160) `1 once the fish in it is the new kind
global EXTINCT_FLOOR = 2 `the fewest kinds that are left dropping in. see THE FLOOR.
global EXTINCT_DROPPING = 0 `how many kinds drop in, from extinctDropping
global dim EXTINCT_LEFT_TIMES(6) `what a swap to the left multiplies the multiplier by, for every rung: 0 for nothing. setup_extinct fills it. see THE LEFT SWAP.
global dim EXTINCT_POPPED(16) `for extinctJudgePops: 1 for every kind that popped in this look
global dim EXTINCT_LEFT(16) `and 1 for every kind that is still on the board

global EXTINCT_CURSOR_OUT = 0 `the rung that the cursor is out on, counted from 1, or 0 when it is on the board
global EXTINCT_CURSOR_EASED# = 0 `how far out the cursor is drawn, from 0 to 1. it chases EXTINCT_CURSOR_OUT.
global EXTINCT_SHAKE_MS = -1 `when the cursor out on the ladder was last shaken, for a swap that does nothing
global EXTINCT_SHAKE_X = 0 `and the way that it was pushed
global EXTINCT_SHAKE_Y = 0

` the swap of a rung, which plays like a swap of two fish before anything happens
global EXTINCT_ACT_MS = -1 `when it started, or -1 when there is none
global EXTINCT_ACT_TIME = 190 `how long the rung takes to slide over, in milliseconds
global EXTINCT_ACT_RUNG = 0 `the rung that is being swapped
global EXTINCT_ACT_WAY = 1 `1 for right, onto the board, and -1 for left

global EXTINCT_POP_AT = -1 `when the board that a flip turned pops, or -1 when there is no flip
global EXTINCT_FLIP_HOLD = 260 `how long the turned board is seen, once it has spun back around, before it pops, in milliseconds

` THE SPIN. a flip turns its rows of the board over like a card, about the line down its middle, with fake
` perspective, and the fish change kind halfway, while the board is edge on (extinctSpinStep). nothing
` can be moved while it spins. only the fish and the cursor spin: coral, ink and the things of a quest
` stay where they are for the moment that it takes.
global EXTINCT_SPIN_MS = -1 `when the spin started, or -1 when there is none
global EXTINCT_SPIN_TIME = 820 `how long the half turn takes, in milliseconds
global EXTINCT_SPIN_DEPTH# = 620 `how far away the eye is, in pixels. smaller is a stronger perspective.
global EXTINCT_SPIN_KIND = 0 `the kind that the board turns into
global EXTINCT_SPIN_TURNED = 0 `1 once the fish have turned into it
global EXTINCT_SPIN_ROW_LO = 0 `the rows that the flip turns, from this one
global EXTINCT_SPIN_ROW_HI = 0 `down to this one
global EXTINCT_QUIET = 0 `1 from a flip until the board has settled, so that the flip's own pops send nothing up the ladder
global EXTINCT_BORN_TIME = 380 `how long a kind takes to slide up onto its rung

global EXTINCT_PREF = 5250 `where the saved game keeps the ladder: a 5, and the three rungs

global EXTINCT_SPRITES_MADE = 0
global dim EXTINCT_FISH_SPRITE(6) `the fish on every rung
global dim EXTINCT_SLOT_SPRITE(6) `the faint box of every rung
global dim EXTINCT_LABEL_TEXT(6) `what a swap to the left gets, in the box to the left of the rungs that have one
global dim EXTINCT_LEFT_SPRITE(6) `the faint box to the left of every rung that a swap that way does something for
global dim EXTINCT_INFO_RUNG(6) `the spot that info mode has for every rung: what a swap to the right does
global dim EXTINCT_INFO_LEFT(6) `and for the box to the left of it: what a swap to the left gets
global EXTINCT_SFX_GONE = 0 `the ping when a kind goes up the ladder
global EXTINCT_SFX_FLIP = 0 `the swell when the board flips
global EXTINCT_SFX_HALVE = 0 `and the low sound when the moves are halved
